{"questions":[{"question_id":"Y02MTkuFNwzuH7VK","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"physics","chapter":"rotational-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"combined-translational-and-rotational-motion","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"the-figure-shows-a-system-consisting-of-i-a-ring-of-outer-2012-marks-4-y02mtkufnwzuh7vk.htm","content":"The figure shows a system consisting of (i) a ring of outer radius 3R rolling clockwise without\nslipping on a horizontal surface with angular speed <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.407ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 622 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and (ii) an inner disc of radius 2R rotating\nanti-clockwise with angular speed <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.991ex\" height=\"2.381ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707.2 879.8 1052.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(263.1,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"639.8\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. The ring and disc are separated by frictionless ball\nbearings. The point P on the inner disc is at a distance R from the origin, where OP makes an\nangle of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.25ex\" height=\"1.649ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -707 1436.6 729\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1033,393.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> with the horizontal. Then with respect to the horizontal surface,<br>\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lzw1awzd/22ee2588-39c5-4f24-9e21-708a289c698b/5db31690-5b6f-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1awze.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1lzw1awzd/22ee2588-39c5-4f24-9e21-708a289c698b/5db31690-5b6f-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1awze.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Rotational Motion Question 68 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1lzw1awzd/22ee2588-39c5-4f24-9e21-708a289c698b/5db31690-5b6f-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1awze.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1lzw1awzd/22ee2588-39c5-4f24-9e21-708a289c698b/5db31690-5b6f-11ef-965d-abded2122fc9/file-jaoe38c1lzw1awze.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.c